How the FPU Works:
The FPU in the Cortex-M4F STM32F407VG MCU is a hardware accelerator that provides floating-point arithmetic functionality. It operates independently of the main CPU, allowing multiple instructions to be executed simultaneously. The FPU consists of registers for storing operands, a pipeline for executing instructions, and a control unit for managing the flow of data.

When the FPU is enabled, it becomes the primary floating-point unit used by the processor. When the FPU is disabled, the processor falls back to using the software emulation for floating-point calculations. The FPU supports a wide range of floating-point instructions, including additions, subtractions, multiplications, divisions, square roots, and trigonometric functions.

